From ddf0bcb7fe07f624a73b58f2fda2f506a0f81dad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hubert Behaghel <behaghel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:46:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve static status labels across publishing and pull

Interpret status and confluence-status links as semantic static labels, never colour URLs. Apply neutral logical styles and carry colour, label spelling, and protocol through named-range metadata with UTF-16-safe splitting of provider text runs.

Use provider range IDs from the existing pre-push fetch to remove changed markers safely. Keep unchanged labels and comments anchored; colour-only edits change styles/metadata without rewriting text. Fail closed on unsupported contexts and unsafe status text merges.

Add 17 regressions covering source/request/import/diff and initial/existing-document async push paths. Full offline suite: 648 tests, 644 expected results, the same four inherited failures. Changed/status functions compile strictly. Live Google conformance is pending.
