diff --git a/README.org b/README.org
index dc2c463..2057fb4 100644
--- a/README.org
+++ b/README.org
@@ -743,6 +743,41 @@ a running UTF-16 insertion index starting at 1 (the beginning of the
 Google Docs body).  This function is used for full document replacement
 and by the diff engine for incremental insertions.
 
+*** Static status labels
+:PROPERTIES:
+:CUSTOM_ID: h:static-status-labels
+:END:
+
+Plain links such as ~[[status:Green][Ready]]~ publish as static coloured
+labels, not colour URLs.  The existing authoring spelling
+~[[confluence-status:Green][Ready]]~ is also accepted and retained on pull.
+Colours are Grey (or Gray), Red, Yellow, Green, Blue, and Purple, matched
+case-insensitively.  Source colour spelling and label text remain intact.
+
+Status runs carry ~:status~ metadata with ~:link-type~, ~:color~, and
+~:described~.  Text styling supplies a neutral background/foreground pair;
+~gdocs-status-COLOR~ entries in ~gdocs-style-definitions~ can override it.
+Semantic named ranges preserve status identity independently of text-run
+splits and styling.  Remote label edits retain the colour and link spelling.
+Provider range IDs are transient diff metadata, not authored Org data.
+
+These labels are not native Google dropdowns.  A static Org status does not
+declare a choice set, so publishing does not invent selectable options.
+Rich labels, tables, footnotes, labels crossing paragraphs, and mixtures
+with native dates or footnotes in one paragraph fail closed.  Imported
+native dropdowns also require an explicit choice-set mapping and are rejected.
+
+Status diffs keep unchanged labels and surrounding text in place.  Colour-only
+changes update styles and semantic ranges without deleting text; removed or
+changed markers are deleted by provider ID before content changes.  A
+simultaneous local/remote status conflict does not fall back to plain-text merge.
+
+Already-published bogus colour URLs are not guessed back into statuses.
+Restore the intended Org status links from a known-good source or backup
+before republishing.  Offline fixtures cover conversion, Unicode ranges,
+provider-run normalization, repeat diffs, and callback source/account handling;
+they do not establish live Google rendering or API conformance.
+
 ** Diff engine
 :PROPERTIES:
 :CUSTOM_ID: h:diff-functions
